<h2>Storage for compact local kitchens</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Drawers under the hob</strong> for vessels, with a cutlery tray and a thali organiser in the top drawer.</li>
  <li><strong>A corner solution</strong> in L-shapes: a carousel or a pull-out corner unit, so the corner does not become dead space.</li>
  <li><strong>A tall pantry unit</strong> beside the fridge for dry groceries, if a 1.5–2 ft wall is free.</li>
  <li><strong>Lofts to the ceiling</strong> with lift-up shutters, for festival vessels and appliances you rarely use.</li>
  <li><strong>A ventilated cylinder cabinet</strong> if you are not on piped gas, kept away from the hob's electrical points.</li>
</ul>
